    description: "**CLUSTER tranch03-cluster-004 (MED confidence) — members F59.A1 + F59.A2.**\n\n**Mechanic**: The producer (linker base class) populates `Edge.derived_from` with the edge's own `[src, dst]` rather than the upstream evidence the linker actually consumed. Two compounded defects flow from this single stub-implementation: (a) Content redundancy — knowing `derived_from` adds no information beyond the edge's own `src`/`dst` fields; the spec's \"Enables answering 'why does this edge exist?' without re-reading linker source code\" resolves to a tautology. Of 23,867 populated rows, 100% match `[edge.src, edge.dst]` in that exact order; 0 reverse order, 0 partial. (b) Structural shape — 47,734 refs (23,867 edges × 2 refs) point at node IDs (100%); 0 point at edge IDs; chain depth distribution is `{0: 86,666, 2: 23,867}` with no length 1, 3, 4 — every chain trace terminates at depth 1 because the target nodes have no further `derived_from`. The \"(or Edge)\" clause is unexercised on the entire corpus.\n\n**Expectation**: `Edge.derived_from` records the actual upstream evidence (decorator AST nodes the linker matched, registry-lookup results, preceding linker-emitted edges) so consumers can answer \"why does this edge exist?\" with information beyond what the edge already carries; refs include edge IDs where appropriate so the relation can chain transitively.\n\n**Scope**: 23,867 of 110,533 edges (21.6%) populated; 100% tautological in content; 100% node-only in target kind. The remaining 86,666 are analyzer-origin and correctly have no `derived_from` (positive control: the structural-presence partition is clean — linkers always populate, analyzers never do).\n\n**Exposure**: Any consumer reading `derived_from` to understand why an edge was emitted; any consumer writing a transitive-provenance traversal expecting PROV `wasDerivedFrom` semantics.\n\n**Consequence**: The provenance promise yields zero net information; transitive traversal always terminates at depth 1; the explain CLI's `--provenance` flag renders the same data as existing relationship lines reformatted, so the flag is output-noise rather than additional signal.\n\n**Source**: CLUSTER (F59.A1 + F59.A2, MED). One linker-base-class refactor — populate `derived_from` with upstream evidence (Symbol or Edge IDs), not `[src, dst]` — addresses both content-redundancy and chain-depth-bounded-to-1 defects.\n\nFiled via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`."  # f39f
    fields: {}  # f39f
